 "summary": "The served-vs-in-process gap is not host overhead: a per-step host timeline (INTARSIA_HOST_PROFILE=1) of the 35B at 16 streams shows a 42.2 ms decode iteration against the 41.6 ms in-process step, 0.07 ms of host work outside the model step and 0.03 ms of GPU idle between steps; steady served decode is 376-390 tok/s against 385. localeval's burst figure divides by a wall that contains the serial prefill of every prompt, which predicts the served 212.6 / 257.1 within 1%. This PR adds the profile knob (measure only) and a one-lock telemetry count per graph replay; knob-unset is neutral against main in an ABAB repeat. The real cost is the burst's serial prefill: PR 137 (stacked, opt-in INTARSIA_PACK_PREFILL=1) packs waiting prompts into one pass: 16 streams 259.7 -> 288.2 tok/s (+11%). HIP busy-chunk stall table in the doc; the default stays 4096 (user decision).",
 "lessons": [
  "Profile before fixing: the stated 5-20 ms host gap did not exist, and the localeval concurrency row includes prefill in its wall, so a served-vs-step comparison needs steady-state decode (stall.py) beside it.",
  "A first A/B can read 2-7% low on one arm from a bimodal per-run state; repeat in ABAB order before believing a regression or a win below 10%.",
  "A packed pass must stay within what plan resolution sized the kernel scratch for (the KV capacity), not only the workspace; the failure only appeared on the real 35B with a small max_seq.",
  "Tests that skip without an env var panic under INTARSIA_REQUIRE_GPU=1: set INTARSIA_QWEN3_DIR too, and remember HIP batching refuses dense models."
